wildos-office (0.1.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Slides, for presentations: LibreOffice Impress with the Wild OS window,
    ribbon, start screen and splash. PowerPoint files open with it and save
    back as .pptx. It is its own package, wildos-slides, and a PC that
    already has Write and Tables gets it once.
  * Ribbon buttons show their short Wild OS names (Picture, Shapes, Page
    break) with British English installed too: LibreOffice's own language
    pack was putting its names back.
  * Removing one of the three apps can no longer stop the others starting:
    each app's own LibreOffice settings now come with that app.

